==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|κιρρός||tawny|tr=kirrhos|lang=grc}} and {{term|-osis|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cirrhoses}}

# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} A chronic disease of the [[liver]] caused by damage from [[toxin]]s (including [[alcohol]]), metabolic problems, [[hepatitis]] or nutritional deprivation. It is characterised by an increase of fibrous tissue and the destruction of liver cells.
# {{context|by extension|lang=en}} Interstitial inflammation of kidneys, lungs, and other organs.
#* {{quote-book|year=1907|author=[[w:Robert W. Chambers|Robert Chambers]]
|chapter=6|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL8127246W The Younger Set]
|passage=“I don't mean all of your friends—only a small proportion—which, however, connects your circle with that deadly, idle, brainless bunch—the insolent chatterers at the opera,{{...}}the speed-mad fugitives from the furies of ennui, the neurotic victims of mental '''cirrhosis''', […]!”}}

